{#
  VRTouchEvents - THE CHOKE BLOCK.                  (2026-09-12, the user's design)

  Up from the moment a choke LANDS - three seconds of held throat - until release
  or passout. Modelled on the DD AddOn's gag block (0795), which works: a hard
  speech constraint delivered as a final instruction on EVERY render, rather than
  as one event that ages out of view.

  The user's stages:
    0-1s   grace, nothing
    1-3s   a grab on the throat - release here is an ordinary short release line
    3s     interrupt + narration, and THIS block comes up
    3-7s   release -> 0797 recovery, 2 renders
    7s     short-lived event + thought for everyone in view
    7-15s  release -> 0797 recovery, 3 renders, severe
    15s    passout; this block goes down with her

  ★ THE STANDING RULE FOR THIS FOLDER (user, 2026-09-08): ENFORCE, DO NOT NEGATE.
    Say what IS true about the body and the output, never what must be avoided -
    a prohibition still describes the forbidden thing, and the model imitates what
    it has just read. The user's draft "you can't break free and are unable to
    breathe" becomes "the grip holds firm against everything she does" and "air
    stops at the grip".
    ⚠ No "do not / never / cannot / can not / no longer" in the RENDERED prose
    below. Comments are exempt. Re-run the check before shipping any edit.

  ⚠ (The old isString(x) and x != "" gate belonged to the decorator designs. A faction rank
    is a real number: a non-member reads below 0, so == 1 is exact.)

  ⚠ render_mode guard: a choke stops SPEECH, not thought. Her inner monologue
    stays free - which is exactly when she has the most to say.

  Numbering: 0796 sits directly after the gag (0795) and before SkyrimNet's
  0800_direct_narration - the same slot that is proven to work for the gag.

  ★★★★ THE GATE IS A LIVE STATE FILE (2026-09-12, fourth design - the user's placeholder idea).
  VRTouchEvents.dll writes Data/SKSE/Plugins/VRTouchEvents/prompt_state.json the instant a
  choke lands (state 1), BEFORE the narration; this reads it with SkyrimNet's read_json, which
  compares the file's modified time on EVERY call and re-reads on a change - so the block is
  current on the very next render. The entry is matched on the SkyrimNet entity UUID, which is
  exactly npc.UUID. Every NPC-data path SkyrimNet has was measured lagging first:
       v1 Papyrus decorator: refreshed 2-3 s AFTER each render - a turn late (2 of 5 right)
       v2 C++ decorator: called live, but the answer reused per NPC for ~30 s - never reached the LLM
       v3 faction rank (get_faction_rank): SkyrimNet's per-NPC game data reused ~20 s after its last
          read - Yamarz (last rendered 21.5 s before) got the block, Carmella (3-20 s) did not
  ⚠ A user_final_instructions FILE is not change-checked (loaded once), so the text itself cannot be
    swapped live - the data it reads can.
  The choker is always the player, so the name is player.name - no decorator at all.
  ⛔ NEVER PIPE A FILTER STRAIGHT OFF A CALL. Upper-casing decnpc(npc.UUID).name directly
     printed the raw expression into her prompt ("rendered with 2 missing variable(s)"). Set
     the value into a variable first, then filter the variable - upper on a set variable
     (_pp in the gag's heading) is the proven form.
  ★★★★★ THE CACHE-BUST (2026-09-13, VR test 5 + the user). SkyrimNet caches EVERY template call by name + argument
  value (55 s default, 30 s from a voice key press), so a plain read_json of this file was served stale on 2 of 7
  renders - the modified-time check inside read_json never runs on a cache hit. The second argument is three
  fresh random values (random is never cached): a number, so read_json ignores it and returns the whole file
  (SkyrimNet.dll 0x697500 - a path is used only when that argument is a string), but it is part of the cache key,
  so nearly every render is a new key and a real read. VERIFIED LIVE 2026-09-13 20:45 (VR test 8, report 45): the DLL wrote the state, the
  render 189 ms later logged 'File modified since cached, reloading' and this block was in that prompt; 22 of 22
  renders in the session ran the read (0 served stale by the callback cache).
  To revert: drop the second argument.
#}
{% if render_mode != "thoughts" and exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") %}
{% set _vs = read_json("VRTouchEvents/prompt_state", random * 10000 + random * 100 + random) %}
{% set _vc_state = 0 %}
{% if isObject(_vs) and existsIn(_vs, "npcs") %}{% for _ve in _vs.npcs %}{% if _ve.uuid == npc.UUID %}{% set _vc_state = _ve.state %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if _vc_state == 1 %}
{% set _vc_by = player.name %}
{% set _p = "he" %}{% set _pp = "his" %}{% set _po = "him" %}
{% if decnpc(npc.UUID).isFemale %}{% set _p = "she" %}{% set _pp = "her" %}{% set _po = "her" %}{% endif %}
{% set _vc_name = decnpc(npc.UUID).name %}
**BEING CHOKED - {{ _vc_name | upper }}'S THROAT IS HELD SHUT.** {{ _vc_by }}'s hand is clamped tight around {{ _pp }} throat right now and holds it closed. Air stops at the grip.

EVERY sound {{ _p }} makes is a choked, strangled noise: gagging, a strangled wheeze, a rasp that dies in the throat. Tone and struggle carry {{ _pp }} whole meaning.

The grip holds firm against everything {{ _p }} does, and it stays exactly this tight until {{ _vc_by }} lets go.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
